## How model lifecycle currently works
- training-service exposes endpoints (notably POST /train and POST /incremental-train).
- training-service persists newly trained/updated models as .pkl into a shared volume path.
- after training, training-service notifies prediction-service via HTTP POST:
  - `http://prediction-service:8000/reload`
- prediction-service keeps an in-memory cache:
  - cache key tracks currently loaded model name
  - GET/POST prediction uses the cached loaded model
  - POST /reload clears cache so the next /predict reloads the .pkl from disk

